From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:52:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Don't jump far away when seeking to prev/next keyframe before
 keyframes are loaded

After jumping to a new location, the keyframes around it are read with a
500ms debounce + ffprobe. Until then, seek prev/next keyframe searched the
whole keyframe cache and could jump to a keyframe from a previously visited,
far away location. Now we track which time ranges have actually been read,
and only seek to a keyframe if the whole range between the current position
and it has been read; otherwise stay put.

Also fix: if a keyframe read was in progress when the user seeked, the read
for the new location was skipped (and the in-progress result discarded), so
keyframes at the new location might never load. Reads are now queued.

Fork-Change: 07-keyframe-seek-before-loaded
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WdW4mLajyN5sfxHVCHh3ao
